  "description": "Storyweave gives each enchantment creature entering in one event two counters and spends itself on that event",
  "note": "CR 614.3 / 608.2f: Storyweave's second mode is the only one offered (alice controls no creature), and its row lasts until used. Two lore counters take Roar of Endless Song from 2 to 4 (main phase gave it its third), so chapter III triggers over the II the main phase raised; II's Elephant token is a creature but no enchantment and leaves the row standing. Replenish returns both Fangs of Shigeki and the sacrificed Roar in one event: each Fang enters with two counters (a row spent by its first entrant gives the second 0), and the row is spent with that event, so a Fang cast afterwards enters with none (2 if the row lasted the turn). Live objects count by name, so the returned Fangs are #2 and #3 behind the one in hand, and the cast one becomes #3 once that hand card is gone.",
